# Production secrets — SOPS-encrypted. Fill values, then:
#   sops -e -i infra/secrets/prod.env    # encrypt in place
# Never commit the plaintext file.
#
# The operator fills these (the lead never types secrets). Values come from
# the accounts listed in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md → Resource access map.
#
# ── "Which mode am I?" decision tree ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Meet needs ONE of two credential sets. Decide before filling:
#
#   OAuth triple (recommended for a single operator mailbox):
#     GOOGLE_MEET_CLIENT_ID + GOOGLE_MEET_CLIENT_SECRET + GOOGLE_MEET_REFRESH_TOKEN
#     → leave GOOGLE_CLIENT_EMAIL / GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY / GOOGLE_IMPERSONATED_USER
#       EMPTY (they are service-account-only).
#
#   Service account (domain-wide delegation):
#     GOOGLE_CLIENT_EMAIL + GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY + GOOGLE_IMPERSONATED_USER
#     → leave the GOOGLE_MEET_* triple EMPTY.
#
# A partial set fails boot loudly (env schema). GOOGLE_MEET_ENABLED=true is
# required to activate either mode.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# --- Core (REQUIRED) ---
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=ENC[AES256_GCM,data:UTkMJqqI2S5BZmX9cDKaaSBRRgORD4+yPV/VW3IhatY=,iv:eSbx5gx4C1z4exjmeR8Mpdi3xYFeHQ8SEP3EhGax4jk=,tag:ggvGpN7PT/Bb/3smDDVpSQ==,type:str]
PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=ENC[AES256_GCM,data:+o6VGVFuIlJv4MZkMaMaKqoYDTiyqhIoR06SjfvrBCdkcueH3DsHxFCMw88=,iv:9ExPUJo/wq7OXhgQQfb4tDEsVrlwMwpTnEQO0pzJCM8=,tag:7HUH1204Ro16ZQcc2ou0eg==,type:str]
